      <activity id="dce43cd6-5e1d-5d1b-b8a9-e465fd4a09d0" activityNameId="507775fc-e355-5c7c-bbd1-b3a39d5d3524" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Cellulose fibre, inclusive blowing in, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Cellulose fibre, inclusive blowing in, at plant
Cellulose fibre in building applications has a density of 50 kg/m3 and a thermal conductivity of 0.04 W/mK when applied. No emissions are inventoried be-sides the heat waste from electricity use for lack of data.;
UUID: a76fddbc-05c5-386e-84f3-d4f1ecad697c
includes the input energy and material to the production processes, transports of the materials and the available process emissions. Also included is the packaging and the energy for the application of the fibres as insulation materi-als in buildings.
Location: production data from one major producer in Switzerland
Technology: mechanical separation of fibres from waste paper
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_a76fddbc-05c5-386e-84f3-d4f1ecad697c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
